    "body": "Module state lookup is generally pretty slow, especially in utility code where we usually have to use the \"fallback\" lookup. For Python 3.13, the Python C API has functions to get the empty constants, and these are likely faster than looking it up through the module state.\n\nAs part of this I've renamed empty `unicode` to `str` and made the names upper-case, largely just to make it easy to generate code that works with both methods of getting the constants.\n\nIt's probably still worth keeping the old lookup if CYTHON_USE_MODULE_STATE isn't set although it's maybe pretty marginal.",
    "closed_at": null,
