                },
                "message": "Don't get constants from module state with CYTHON_USE_MODULE_STATE\n\nModule state lookup is generally pretty slow, especially in utility\ncode where we usually have to use the \"fallback\" lookup.\nFor Python 3.13, the Python C API has functions to get the\nempty constants, and these are likely faster than looking it up\nthrough the module state.\n\nAs part of this I've renamed empty `unicode` to `str` and made\nthe names upper-case, largely just to make it easy to generate\ncode that works with both methods of getting the constants.\n\nIt's probably still worth keeping the old lookup if\nCYTHON_USE_MODULE_STATE isn't set although it's maybe pretty marginal.",
